EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Constantinople_TheoderetOfHouseCriamon" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Theoderet of House Criamon"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Theoderet of House Criamon (Chapter Seven: Constantinople, p102): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t9c6ebf8eb7f82a5388727f ^"Theoderet of House Criamon" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t1279ab0ebf8d87bf54c40f ^"Xylinites"]
            ^"Age" STRING "75 (Apparent Age: 43)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Pious +3, Fatalistic +1, Reclusive +1. Born to a Maronite family in the Lebanon, and apprenticed late in life, some years after his Gauntlet Theoderet was delighted to receive word of the establishment of a Clutch in the Tribunal of Thebes. Fluent in Syriac and Aramaic, his Greek remains heavily accented. Filthy and ragged, but well versed in etiquette, he is a terrifying figure, and one whose talents and obvious discretion, while appreciated by polite society, do not earn him friends. This is, of course, exactly how he likes it. He is official castrator for the orphanage, and because of his known medical skills he has been called upon many times to conduct blindings at the palace and throughout the city. With Deft Art Corpus, and as a master of Perdo Corpus magic, he uses primarily magical means to painlessly and safely conduct these duties. He is philosophically committed to his work, seeing it as helping to establish Harmony where the likely alternative of execution or murder in many instances would simply bring more Strife into the world."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 102
        }
    }

}
